  "authoringNote": "D1 accept contrast (review finding 1). Encounter narrative and supporting-note text were unrestricted strings in v1 and stay unrestricted: empty and whitespace-only values are valid exact bodies and are kept byte for byte (the payload hashes in the manifest pin them). They are not evidence fields, so no rule cites them and no exactText entry is possible; preservation is proven by the pinned bytes. Each of the four versions would otherwise get its own R09 body_invalid condition, so a wrong nonblank rule is observable: R09 passes with no condition. Both final encounters state 2026-08-20, so they agree (no encounters_disagree), and each pairs with the final order 2026-09-02 (same identifier, sequenced, within bound): R04 passes citing three facts of each encounter and three of the order (nine). R02 binds all six subject-scoped versions and cites their names and identifiers (twelve). R06 cites both encounters' five clinical statements (ten); R07 cites both false LCMP flags. R01, R03 and R05 are ordinary (eight, nine and four citations). State ready_for_review.",
